[{:db/id 17592186152126 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39fe4419-4a43-50fa-a07c-6ab5298bae4f" "question-46c072ed-28fe-5e0e-96d0-a316d330f872"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-39fe4419-4a43-50fa-a07c-6ab5298bae4f" :question/id #uuid "39fe4419-4a43-50fa-a07c-6ab5298bae4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-67819" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\frac{1}{10}$ is natural number\n\nII. $\\frac{1}{10}$ is an integer\n\nIII. $\\frac{1}{10}$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of all numbers that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is not an integer.\n\n- $\\frac{1}{10}$ is a rational number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6ddb88e1-f38e-5794-a535-77e7876e74f5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6ddb88e1-f38e-5794-a535-77e7876e74f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ddb88e1-f38e-5794-a535-77e7876e74f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-138bd42d-bdd5-5103-a741-25924bfa0d76" :answer-field/choices ["answer-899c20e5-4344-5547-829c-68e151ee1feb" "answer-739cdf7c-1cac-5a34-beb6-6fa4499d7934" "answer-e15793bd-544a-5738-b2d9-b9df1c36295d" "answer-40048675-6488-5fe3-b64d-e1be872b48eb" "answer-138bd42d-bdd5-5103-a741-25924bfa0d76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-899c20e5-4344-5547-829c-68e151ee1feb" :answer/id #uuid "899c20e5-4344-5547-829c-68e151ee1feb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-739cdf7c-1cac-5a34-beb6-6fa4499d7934" :answer/id #uuid "739cdf7c-1cac-5a34-beb6-6fa4499d7934" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e15793bd-544a-5738-b2d9-b9df1c36295d" :answer/id #uuid "e15793bd-544a-5738-b2d9-b9df1c36295d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-40048675-6488-5fe3-b64d-e1be872b48eb" :answer/id #uuid "40048675-6488-5fe3-b64d-e1be872b48eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-138bd42d-bdd5-5103-a741-25924bfa0d76" :answer/id #uuid "138bd42d-bdd5-5103-a741-25924bfa0d76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46c072ed-28fe-5e0e-96d0-a316d330f872" :question/id #uuid "46c072ed-28fe-5e0e-96d0-a316d330f872" :question/math-academy-id "q-93611" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-10$ is a natural number\n\nII. $-10$ is an integer\n\nIII. $-10$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of all numbers that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $-10$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $-10$ is an integer.\n\n- $-10$ is a rational number because it can be written as $\\frac{(-10)}{1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4cd1f0fa-8af8-54fb-b456-0eee7ce3fb92"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4cd1f0fa-8af8-54fb-b456-0eee7ce3fb92" :answer-field/id #uuid "