ole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $-3$ and $5$ are integers, but $\\frac{3}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2e18ef21-c07b-584b-a353-bc2e107acf2e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2e18ef21-c07b-584b-a353-bc2e107acf2e" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e18ef21-c07b-584b-a353-bc2e107acf2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77a50393-7099-5a74-b6fa-5abc6300ec01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75c7099d-8ae5-5ce9-8677-484e3279c83b" "answer-57a6471b-bd77-5aee-aeff-e9d5f4387baf" "answer-66d9b2ee-4fe7-59c8-9132-d913e4e61062" "answer-77a50393-7099-5a74-b6fa-5abc6300ec01" "answer-b3c8f7ea-0cb0-5b68-9325-dd9c3a2362cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75c7099d-8ae5-5ce9-8677-484e3279c83b" :answer/id #uuid "75c7099d-8ae5-5ce9-8677-484e3279c83b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57a6471b-bd77-5aee-aeff-e9d5f4387baf" :answer/id #uuid "57a6471b-bd77-5aee-aeff-e9d5f4387baf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66d9b2ee-4fe7-59c8-9132-d913e4e61062" :answer/id #uuid "66d9b2ee-4fe7-59c8-9132-d913e4e61062" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77a50393-7099-5a74-b6fa-5abc6300ec01" :answer/id #uuid "77a50393-7099-5a74-b6fa-5abc6300ec01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3c8f7ea-0cb0-5b68-9325-dd9c3a2362cd" :answer/id #uuid "b3c8f7ea-0cb0-5b68-9325-dd9c3a2362cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152878 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-2$ is a natural number\n\nII. $-2$ is an integer\n\nIII. $-2$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall our definitions.\n\n- The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers: $1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…$\n\n- The integers consist of all of the positive and negative whole numbers, and zero: $…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…$\n\n- The rationals consist of any number that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $-2$ is not a natural number.\n\n- $-2$ is an integer.\n\n- $-2$ is a rational number because it can be written as $\\frac{(-2)}{1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151775 :answer-field/correct 17592186151780 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-eb2e9e07-c134-569e-a208-041621377fa3" :question/id #uuid "eb2e9e07-c134-569e-a208-041621377fa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-99311" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are integers?\n\nI. $100$\n\nII. $-5$\n\nIII. $-\\frac{9}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The integers consist of all positive and negative whole numbers and zero.\n\n$$\n…,-3,\\,-2,\\,-1,\\,0,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,…\n$$\n\n \n\nOf the given numbers, $100$ and $-5$ are integers, but $-\\frac{9}{2}$ is not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-189f8c27-4698-52fa-b757-7d2b24c8aa2a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-189f8c27-4698-52fa-b757-7d2b24c8aa2a" :answer-field/id #uuid "189f8c27-4698-52fa-b757-7d2b24c8aa2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-99522998-d655-5aee-9ba1-5f3e13bc3006" :answer-field/choices ["answer-99522998-d655-5aee-9ba1-5f3e13bc3006" "answer-5a5526aa-d152-5495-bbcb-6f1e1ee